<DetailLayout title="How to Book China Trains" subtitle="The 12306 system, Trip.com alternative, ticket classes, seat selection, and a step-by-step guide to navigating Chinese train stations."
  description="How to book China train tickets as a foreigner: Trip.com vs 12306 step-by-step, ticket classes, seat selection, and what to expect at the station.">
  <h2>The Two Ways to Book</h2>
  <h3>Option 1: Trip.com (Easiest for Foreigners)</h3>
  <p>Trip.com (formerly Ctrip) has an English interface and accepts foreign credit cards. You can book high-speed and regular trains through their app or website. They charge a small booking fee (usually 20-30 RMB per ticket) but the English interface and foreign card support make it worth it for most travelers.</p>
  <h4>Step-by-Step on Trip.com</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the Trip.com app or website and select "Trains"</li>
    <li>Enter your departure and arrival cities — use English names (e.g., "Guangzhou" not "Guangzhou South" at first, you'll pick the specific station later)</li>
    <li>Select your date. Trains open for booking 15 days ahead</li>
    <li>Browse the results — each listing shows duration, departure/arrival time, and ticket class prices</li>
    <li>Pick your class: Second Class for budget, First Class for comfort on longer trips</li>
    <li>Enter passenger details <strong>exactly</strong> as they appear on your passport. One typo and you won't board</li>
    <li>Pay with your foreign card. Trip.com charges in your home currency</li>
    <li>You'll receive a confirmation email with a pick-up code. At the station, go to the ticket counter with your passport and the code to collect your physical ticket</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Option 2: 12306 (Official, Cheaper, Harder)</h3>
  <p>The official China Railway app and website (12306.cn) has an English version. It's cheaper (no booking fee) and tickets are available slightly earlier than on third-party sites. However, the interface can be frustrating, and foreign card acceptance is inconsistent. If you read some Chinese or are patient, it's the best option for frequent travelers.</p>
  <h4>12306 Registration Tips</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Download the "Railway 12306" app (English version available)</li>
    <li>Register with your passport number — the name fields must match your passport character-for-character</li>
    <li>If foreign card payment fails (common), try a different card or fall back to Trip.com</li>
    <li>Once registered, you can buy up to 4 tickets per order</li>
  </ol>

